2. The initial silhouette only shows the Aniimo's identifying features; the rest remain hidden. Pathfinders can reveal the concealed parts by taking photos of Aniimo that share the same features as the mystery Aniimo.
3. Take and submit a photo of an Aniimo in the form depicted by the silhouette to complete the research topic and claim the corresponding rewards. Successfully photographing the Aniimo before the full silhouette is revealed grants an additional Aniimo observation reward!
4. Pathfinders can also submit eligible photos from their existing album. If a photo contains the mystery Aniimo, it counts toward completing the event.
5. Pay attention to Aniimo forms. Only photos showing the same form as the mystery Aniimo will count toward event completion.
6. Photos of your own Aniimo, other players' Aniimo, and wild Aniimo in Idyll can all be used to complete the event.
7. Aniimo in the Holo-Battle Sim are holographic projections, and Aniimo in the Sanctums come from ancient seals. Photos of Aniimo in these locations cannot be recognized for submission.<color=#81D67B>Hug ■■ hug ■■ hug ■■ hug—</color>How can you obtain <style=Hint_BgD>Runes</style> that enhance an Aniimo's Carried Item stats?Custom MarkerI can feel his powerful magic aura. He must be amazing! Chrrr!
