Twenty
I spent my twentieth birthday with Tucker.
It was a rare sunny day in the Mistwoods. We met at the <style=Hint_BgD>old spot</style>.
Tucker loves burying itself there. No one but me can get it out.
We planned this celebration ages ago.
Mistwoods, brace for the cursed duet!
...
All the Witchins having a music party covered their ears and ran.
Our cursed singing won again!
...
Even the Pomeggs, who love crowds, ran away.
...
I looked around. Not a single Hummin left.
...
We really made everyone in the Mistwoods listen to our song!
Though I bet no one knew it was “Happy Birthday.”
...
I used to hate singing birthday songs and celebrating birthdays.
I’ve always been tone-deaf and would get laughed at.
But singing with Tucker makes me happy, even though everyone in the Mistwoods hates it.
I’m looking forward to my next birthday.
And the next, and the next, and the next... I’m spending them all with Tucker!Thank you! You’re a good Susuta!You don't have enough training coinsYoung people have so many ideas. I could never come up with as many perfume concepts as Sunia...
No wonder Lady Irelia favors her the most.This exhibition is amazing! I got a whole bag full of material for my paper!Sunshade Water LilyStrange Energy flow... Glimmer Tree... where does it all lead in the end...45<color=#5090df>%s</color> tossed fruit peel on <color=#5090df>%s's</color> head, which led to a huge fight that ends with <color=#5090df>%s</color> being beaten up.Dance among the flowers, and every step carries their scent.For generations, Glynseras and Scorchhowls have been leading their families to fight against each other for control of Beast Fang Ridge, and even the young Boneskies and Emberpups were involved. A Bonesky accidentally fell off a cliff during a battle and broke its leg. An Emberpup rescued it and sent it back. The Bonesky didn't understand why the Emberpup would help an enemy, but according to the Emberpup, it simply didn't want its future mortal enemy to die like this. Touched by the sincerity and fighting spirit, they made a pact to become the best of their own species and have the final duel to decide who is the most powerful one on Beast Fang Ridge. Since then, they went on different paths in search of power, and you were the witness of the pact. At the end of the story, the Bonesky grew into the most powerful Glynsera, Recas, and the broken leg became its weapon for harvesting glories. But the Emberpup never showed up for the duel. The loneliness ate Recas alive, making it understand that the price of being the most powerful one is more than just scars and a broken leg, but also loneliness.Pebble PavingAuto-AimNo, that’s not it! I wanted to see you myself!So why not stock up on some Aniipods?Journey DelightsBINI’s photo and my drawing match perfectly, don’t they?Insomniac CubboThe final hit of the basic attack will Mark the target on the farther side with <style=Hint_BgL>[Sludge]</style>. When a Skill ATK hits the Marked side, it removes the Mark, dealing <style=Hint_BgL>25</style> Might Damage and applying <style=Hint_BgL>8</style> stacks of <style=Hint_BgL><link="source_8038"><u>[Water Abnormal Status]</u></link></style> to self.Enter group chat name.Ugh...Do you also wish to become—
