Tap the <style=Hint_BgL>Throw button</style> to toss it, tap the <style=Hint_BgL>Drop button</style> to put it down.Bathes in moonlight and recovers <style=Hint_BgL>20</style> EP.Little 6Use Flutternym Scales.SunnyIn Awen’s childhood memories, her home was just like any ordinary family home in Bloomville—simple, warm, and familiar. Back then, the biggest problem in her life seemed to be that her mother would stay out in the flower fields to cultivate new varieties instead of coming home, while her father’s complaints gave Awen no end of headaches.
Even when she sensed that she was somehow different from the other people of Bloomville, it never troubled her too deeply.
She learned flower cultivation and perfumery from her mother, while her younger sister Aria was obsessed with Adventures of the Direfin Warband, a book left behind by their grandmother, and showed great enthusiasm for becoming a writer.
Only when rare snow fell over the Sea of Flowers would their mother gaze toward its deepest reaches with a wistful look in her eyes.
Young Awen once asked her mother what lay beyond the Sea of Flowers.
Her mother told her that her homeland was in that white sea of flowers.
Awen asked why she did not go back to visit.
Her mother only said, “It’s snowing, but my homeland isn’t there anymore.”
As Awen grew older, she gradually realized that the scent she carried was different from that of ordinary Bloomville residents.
She wanted to find the homeland her mother had spoken of, to find the “origin” she had never visited.
At last, after braving countless dangers, she reached the ancient white perfume tower deep within the Sea of Flowers.
There, she discovered that Rosetower Woods was where her mother had been born.
But her own “difference” did not come from Rosetower Woods. It came from the fact that her grandparents were from Azureville.
Awen thought: she had to leave this place and go toward her origin.
As for her younger sister Aria, home was a place one was destined to leave. To leave home was to begin anew.
For Awen, home was a guiding scent, leading her toward the place she came from.Open Home Building - Material ProcessingAccidentally made Nimbi angry again...Equipped with a comfortable power supply platform customized for aniimo, it effectively solves the energy consumption issue during Aniipod production.Whenever this mysterious mage appears, Celestis can't help but gather around and follow along.Complete the objective within 90sLighting RangeAniimo family investigation completedMission ItemHelmonSignificantly increases defense against <style=Hint_BgL>enemies of Nightmare difficulty and below</style>.
