irty-eight charactersThe lost FlutternymExtremely rare rose with dual mutations, enveloped in a rainbow-like glow while sparkling with dazzling spots of light.My Flameruff’s fire has faded... but the embers it left behind await the most mysterious revival!Skip battle phaseTwine to become a Pawney first.Do you really want to release an uncommon Aniimo?Tower Climb Sweep RewardsI'm back!Let's keep it short!Ugh! What an annoying Aeon! Why does he never answer anything?!Premium SectionOne pull, one jackpot!I am heading to Idyll for a promotional shoot and need outfits that can be easily adjusted for the best results.Very goodShellTell Sayn about...Yay Yay YayJourney of Trials Furniture PackAbsorbs all puddles within <style=Hint_BgL>10</style> m. Each puddle absorbed heals the whole team for <style=Hint_BgL><customRichText(calcData,ability,11730410,param1,1,%d)>%</style> of own max HP. Absorbs up to <style=Hint_BgL>4</style> puddles at once.A jade-carved figurine with a smooth, lustrous finish.Save failed, System storage space insufficientWhy become a Lethal Thorn? To protect... but protect what exactly?SeesawChapter 5: Flowers and Thorns
The earth trembled, and flowers withered.
With the loss of the whitesnow rose and Cubbo’s roses, the forest descended into chaos and violence.
All the Cubbos and Grizbos woke up.
They roared and rampaged through the forest. Peace was no more.
...
The Bloomville villagers fled from Rosetower Woods.
They brought some Budsquire refugees with them.
To ensure the survival of Budsquires in the world, Princess Melloblum entrusted the care of the Budsquires to Bloomville.
...
Armand did not retreat with the Bloomville villagers.
He was the First Lethal Thorn of the Seven Lethal Thorns! How could he abandon Princess Melloblum?
But he could only watch, helpless, as his companions fell one by one in the onslaught. He hated how powerless he was.
It was then that Princess Melloblum said to him, “Armand, rest now, you’ve done well.”
He watched as Princess Melloblum performed that familiar Dance of Blissful Bloom.
The dance gave the Budsquires enough strength to retreat into the Maze of Thorns.
After entrusting her daughter, the little princess, to Armand, Princess Melloblum fell at last.
————
