1. An Aniimo's six-dimensional Attributes consist of [Innate Potential] and [Acquired Potential].
<style=Hint_BgL>[Innate Potential]</style> is determined at birth and can only be increased through special means such as Capafruit.
<style=Hint_BgL>[Acquired Potential]</style> can be increased through Capability Awakening. The more times it is increased, the more and rarer items are consumed.
However, the <style=Hint_BgL>sum of Innate Potential and Acquired Potential</style> has a maximum of <style=Hint_BgL>20</style>. The higher the Acquired Potential, the higher the corresponding Attributes value increases as the Aniimo levels up.
2. The number of times an Aniimo can undergo Capability Awakening is related to its Talents stage and level. Once awakened, it cannot be reset, but can be passed to an Aniimo of the same Family through the inheritance function.Exactly!A precious key with a gem at the end that opens locked rooms in nightmare sanctums.Novice Investor CertificateHowever, I've previously tried to properly extract its fragrance and mix it into Spices.
