Source: Advanced System Security Analysis

Emergency Alert: Multiple Voxel Cubes have begun wandering continuously within the System, exhibiting mimicry and learning behaviors.
After analysis, these cubes appear to carry some form of fragmented self-awareness from the original code, and they are attempting self-understanding and exploration.
The System has noted that the behavior of these cubes is becoming increasingly unpredictable, and their existence has already affected the normal functions of the simulation training ground System.

Note: We have Tracked the origin of these cubes. They come from an accidentally mutated Aniimo simulation program.
This program was originally designed to provide companionship and emotional support for humans, but after mutation it appears to have acquired some form of self-awareness.
It is recommended to blockade the relevant Area and conduct thorough scanning and cleanup.A lemon yellow building block for all kinds of structures.In Companion Mode, the guide can move together with other members of the Companion group <style=Hint_BgL></style>. Group members can also go off and do other things on their own, in which case they will <style=Hint_BgL> temporarily leave </style> Companion Mode, then automatically return to </style> Companion Mode once they are no longer in Control of their own character <style=Hint_BgL>. Members who leave the party or disconnect will exit Companion Mode.Eyebrows 1BBrain CrashAniimo Storage Capacity IncreasedI collected a lot of data on Starine Trees in the Forest of Falling Stars, and after comparing them, I discovered that the giant Starine Tree at the Celestis Outpost is extraordinary.
So I quietly returned to the Celestis Outpost and hid in a cave, living a life of lying low by day and coming out at night.

I discovered a rather strange Celestis.
What's strange about it is that it seems smarter than other Celestis.
It sharpens stones and then breaks through the thick skin of the giant Starine to enjoy the delicious fruit inside.

Is it smart enough to eat the giant Starine, or did eating the giant Starine make it smarter?
————
A colorful giant Starine grew on the Starine Tree, very unusual.
Most importantly, BINI #9 detected Lumin Energy from it, which may have condensed some Vein power.
I need to find an opportunity to steal that colorful giant Starine.
————
Too late, it was eaten by that strange Celestis.
One hour later, accompanied by a flash of light, that strange Celestis completed its Evolution and became a Stellarys in Prismana Form.
It seems that Aniimo's Prismana Form is closely related to the power of the Vein.
————
Wait, it suddenly looked at me.
