choosing to carry their memories with them in search of new hope.
Cities collapsed, records were sealed away, and this planet was written into history—becoming what would come to be known as “home.”What was once a complete notebook has now become scattered pages. The varying degree of damage and different handwriting among the pages suggest that they were written at different times across a long period.
Perhaps the writer was not very diligent, leaving behind only a handful of entries over the years.
Yet these fragments are traces of his time—weathered but vivid.
