Twenty
I spent my twentieth birthday with <color=#ffe451>Tucker</color>.
It was a rare sunny day in the Mistwoods. We met at the old spot.
Tucker loves burying itself there. No one but me can get him out.
I was happy, not just because Tucker shared its favorite truffles, but because I had good news.
I was chosen by a caravan, and they offered me the opportunity to go somewhere far away.
But when I told Tucker about this, it didn’t seem to care about what “far away” meant to me.
But it was all I could think about.
Back then, I had no idea how long it would take to get there and when I would come back.
I bet it didn’t know either, since “far away” probably just meant the furthest place its vines could reach.So disappointed.Archival Chip - Mural of Infergon's Birth(Translator) It’s the only one who can sing basso.They all exist side by side... like the tones of this dew—blended, yet unchanged. They don’t become each other... I think... I understand now.It’s finally over... That was exhausting... Wait!Tilt CameraWarmThe sun pattern and Lun pattern on it emit a faint glow.
