A plant of the Asteraceae family with bright Uncommon leaves in a spoon shape. Delicate stems bear flowers about the size of a thumb.
Found in well-lit environments, Common, pink, and yellow Blossoms are commonly seen.
Starsprout Daisies are remarkably resilient; once planted, they can withstand light Aniimo trampling, making them excellent candidates as lawn alternatives.

Millebloom Lotus
A plant of the Nelumbonaceae family, an aquatic flower. With abundant Petals and magnificent Form, it often grows alongside schools of Skippy fish.
Its lotus seeds and roots have a bitter taste, rarely used in human cuisine, but are quite favored by Water Aniimo.
The rhizomes are often made into sachets in summer, serving as excellent mosquito repellent material.

Blisswort
A shrub family plant, commonly found on the high rooftops of Bloomville. Low in ornamental value, yet it is the third most demanded Perfumery material in Bloomville.
Blisswort itself is odorless, but its processed juice has extremely strong scent-diffusing Abilities.
A single Iris flower combined with Blisswort juice can produce a fragrance even more intense than a cluster of Iris flowers.
It's called Blisswort precisely because it greatly resolved the worry of Perfumery masters about insufficient raw materials.
