Fifty
I came back to the Mistwoods anyway,
But not to the usual spot.
Not because I couldn’t find the way; I just avoided it.
I kept going over my stories about those places far away,
As if telling the stories would make up for leaving it for so long.
Then it hit me—Tucker never liked “far away.”
So I became a truffle trader.
I thought maybe I could come to Tucker with the best truffles I could find and wake it up and tell it:
“Rise and shine, Tucker, or I’m going to eat all the truffles myself!”
But I haven’t found the best truffles yet.
No matter how much I raised the price, the truffle hunter returned with fewer and fewer truffles each time.
