<style=Hint_BgL>Battle Phase</style>: Pathfinders defeat the enraged Legendary Aniimo, then enter the <style=Hint_BgL>Soothing Phase</style>.

<style=Hint_BgL>Soothing Phase</style>: Pathfinders Throw Aniipods to help the Legendary Aniimo regain calm and earn affection. During this process, there's a chance to win item rewards and gain the recognition and companionship of the Legendary Aniimo!Eee, haaa—If the speed of time flow is slowed down, one should be able to pass through the Wind fan.When he was young, Baboni would always ask his mentor Avetine why the legendary perfume formula was called “Golden Wish” and why its main ingredient was named “Golden Answer.” Avetine would tell him the story of Haidt, the founding perfumer.
————
Haidt was a genius perfumer, and also a strange one.
She always lived in her own world. Perfumery was her way of speaking to the world, and fragrance was the world’s response.
She could hear others, yet never quite understood them.
It was as if her ears caught the words, but her heart could not truly listen.
In search of inspiration, Haidt came to Blitzwood, where she was struck by lightning and fell unconscious.
After waking up, she found herself in a cave beneath a Blitz Tree. She was brought there by a Blazen. A young, clueless Bolty was also there.
Haidt could not understand them.
Then the Blazen motioned for her to touch its bristling tail.
A faint yet layered current of electricity flowed through her.
Haidt withdrew her hand instinctively, but a word echoed in her heart:
Concern.
She could not understand the words, yet for the first time she felt the meaning of concern.
Injured and touched by this feeling, Haidt stayed—living with the Blazen and its cub.
They grew from strangers into family.
Haidt would often go with the Blazen to the Blitz Tree.
The Blazen would send its wishes to the World of Wonders through electric currents, and would also carry Haidt’s voice into the world.
The thunder rolled on as usual, but nothing ever came of it.
The little Bolty was not interested in this routine, as if it did not believe in the World of Wonders at all.
So the days passed on.
Until one day, the Blazen left—perhaps to the World of Wonders.
Haidt went to the Blitz Tree one last time.
She could not generate electricity, but she cried out from the very bottom of her heart.
A peal of thunder sounded, and a branch fell—like a reply from a distant friend.
————
Young Baboni was deeply drawn to Haidt’s amazing story. He too longed to see that World of Wonders.
Each time, Avetine would shake her head gently and call him her “silly little apprentice.”
Baboni grew frustrated.
He began to feel that perhaps Avetine didn’t really like him, especially when she mentioned that once he finished his studies here, she would leave for a long journey. Baboni felt sad and was convinced that she just couldn’t wait to leave her foolish apprentice.
It was only when he crafted Golden Wish that Baboni understood—what Avetine truly wished was for him to grow into an apprentice she could trust and let go, and that Haidt had not named that fallen branch Golden Answer because the branch itself is amazing.
Perhaps that thunder was not truly a reply from her friend Blazen.
But the bond they once shared would never fade.Condense water at the target's feet to unleash a Water Rush at the target.The locked-on target is too far away. Try <style=Hint_BgL>moving in to attack</style> or <style=Hint_BgL>switching targets</style>.Hey, are you okay?Fun Blind BoxHome Power SystemAdequateLet me talk some sense into it. A wooden Susuta figurine with lovingly carved dark circles under its eyes. Sleep-deprived, adorable, and crafted with real care.I just finished preparing, don't worry.
