Source: Simulated Training Ground System Abnormal Status Report

Multiple autonomously generated Voxel Cubes have been detected within the System.
These cubes are gradually increasing in number and possess a certain degree of mobility.
More surprisingly, there appear to be signs of some form of connection and communication between these cubes.
Preliminary assessment indicates that these cubes are anomalously generated by the code simulating Aniimo, but their behavior exceeds expectations.
Further Field Notes are needed regarding the generation mechanism of these cubes and whether they will have a negative impact on the stability of the Simulated Training Ground System.Need to gather nectar before sunset, must hurry!What is this Aniimo? It looks really impressive.Happy...<style=Hint_BgL>Don't know what to do with excess</style>items? You can sell them in your<style=Hint_BgL>Inventory</style>, and you'll receive<style=Hint_BgL>Credits</style>after selling. Note! Sold items cannot be recovered.Aniimo Training Level Cap BreakthroughChest thief! Get them, little Whelpies!The Glamour Star Auditions are open! Dress up your Aniimo according to the theme and aim for a high score to become the brightest star!A Bloom filled with Vein energy, which can be approached and the <style=Hint_BgL>Aniimo Bonding</style> function used. It will continuously attract large numbers of Aniimo to appear, a phenomenon known as <style=Hint_BgL>Group Appearance</style>. During this phase, <style=Hint_BgL>Catching</style> these Aniimo allows the Bloom to accumulate <style=Hint_BgL>Prismana Energy</style>.Correct. Hope you can have a good achievement in an actual Holo-Battle Sim.*Electric currents leap* Lighthouse... you want to be the light that shines in the darkness, waiting and hoping?If you get 2 matching results, you'll receive 3 Voxel Cubes; if you get 3 matching results...CaveCome with me, I'll take you to see Uncle!
