————
After leaving the Celestis outpost, I saw a very tall Starine tree in the distance.
1. Starines
2. A high place
3. A solitary living space
All the information tells me that it must be where the Stellarys lives.
While retaining their love for Starines and high places (as members of the Celestis family), Stellaryses prefer to live alone and keep out of sight.
My following research will focus on the reason for such a peculiar trait.
————
Based on my observations, compared to Celestises, Stellaryses have significantly increased dark energy.
Combined with the information I found at the Celestis outpost, my assumption has been proven.
Stellaryses are intelligent beings to some extent. Despite the fact that they still belong to the same family as Celestises, they become, at some point, two different life forms. Aniimo are just so amazing.[In the woods northwest of Mistwoods]Wanna practice climbing? Go use the pillars and walls across the way!5 Mutual FriendsThe Sea of Flowers has become more lush and beautiful in recent years, and it’s all thanks to Lady Irelia’s blessing. The quality of our aromathyst harvest has never been better!Right... I’ll probably end up taking a beating, and that might get me down for a while... but no friendship is perfect.5 seconds after combat begins, a pulse crystal is generated on the field. After a 3-second delay, it fires a pulse ATK, triggering once every 15 seconds. It does not trigger when enemies are in Break State. The pulse deals Damage and knockback to Pathfinders and can be blocked by enemies. When it hits an enemy, it deals <customRichText(calcData,timeline,2030101,param1,1,%d)>% BREAK value and increases Damage taken by <customRichText(calcData,buff,4003011,param0,1,%d)>% Over Time for <customRichText(buffConfigData,4003011,duration)> seconds.Your Dragonsbreath Mocha has arrived, enjoy.Golden Wish paints the pale dreamscape with the color of miracles.Using a Counter Mark to deal damage has a 50% chance to instantly gain 10 EP.You're welcome...Every <style=Hint_BgL><customRichText(calcData,buff,9126301,param0,1)></style>s, the next skill applies <style=Hint_BgL>1</style> stack of <style=Hint_BgL><link="source_8028"><u>[Drowsiness]</u></link></style> to the target.Unlocks upon completing the story [Waves and the Song of Wonder]Exit spectating and go to results?Woof! Ruff!Unclaimed ChestA pack that can be purchased at RV level <style=Hint_BgL>3</style>.Summon the IrisalisStrange thing?Add BonusNear the shore where the Sherro vanished, a few Susutas were peeking around.
