Soon after, Armand returned to Bloomville to tell his tale of discovery in Beardow Woods.
All who heard his tale were excited about the miraculous seedling.
Especially the perfumers, who wanted to ride the long winds of the Gryphon God directly to Beardow Woods and see the miraculous seedling for themselves.
...
The perfumers, fragrant and singing, arrived at Beardow Woods in high spirits.
They built a towering perfumery near the miraculous seedling, and fragrance wafted from the tower.
With the perfumers’ care and nurturing, the miraculous seedling grew amazingly well.
Incredibly, contact with the miraculous seedling’s vines allowed a Budsquire to learn the power of [Thorns].
The Thornblades swore fealty to Princess Melloblum.
A beautiful sentiment and a pure bond was formed.
...
Soon, Princess Melloblum had seven powerful Thornblades in her service.
Yes, not six, but seven Thornblades. 
