Do you think—Aniimo Accessory Slot ExpansionLavender BlossomInteraction ZoneJust how strong is the First Lethal Thorn?Rookey Ambience SFX - Combat EntryFirst Stop: Bloom Festival
Upon arriving at Bloomville, I was fortunate to participate in a grand celebration called the "Bloom Festival."
From the day the dedication ceremony is held, Bloomville experiences a colorful flower rain lasting three Sols, vibrant and dreamlike.
Thousands of Blossoms compete in full bloom, each swaying gracefully in the breeze. Petals drift down lightly, landing on my shoulders and hair, bringing a hint of coolness and fragrance.
In that moment, I felt as though I had stepped into a fairy tale World...

Second Stop: Irisalis
After the dedication ceremony, I had the honor of meeting Bloomville's Guardian—the Legendary Aniimo, Irisalis.
She stood quietly amidst the sea of Blossoms. Though she appeared quite pale after bringing down the flower rain, she remained awe-inspiring.
Locals say that she falls into slumber after each ceremony, and when the next ceremony begins, she blooms once more with brilliant colors.
The cycle and Wondrous nature of HP is like the Blooming and falling of flowers in Bloomville—everything proceeds in nature's rhythm.
Regrettably, another powerful Aniimo, Somniwing, did not appear. Perhaps I'll have the chance to meet her on my next visit.

Third Stop: Blossom Sea
Today I visited the Blossom Sea and experienced Bloomville's unique Perfumery craft.
The flower rain brought by Irisalis continues to this Sol. Amidst the falling petals, people gather Blossoms of various colors and feed them to Dewy. These adorable little sprites transform the floral fragrance into aromatic incense.
I personally took part, with the fluffy Dewy nestling intimately into my palm. On the Idyll Continent, humans and Aniimo coexist in such harmony.
With some trial and error, I created a bottle of stress-relief fragrance. Taking a gentle whiff, that fresh and elegant scent instantly permeated my lungs. In that instant, it seemed to wash away all worries and fatigue...
