ite at night to explore the mystery of the whale bonesPlace a woodland plot in your Home.Bloom: Echoback LandingUnder the gaze of countless travelers, the ruins by the roadside have stood quietly for a thousand years, untouched by wind, rain, or lightning.Talk to Fannie outside the Co-op Store.There seems to be some kind of magical architectureLeave the elder’s house and go to the Bloom Festival.="This is"&J67&", detailed instructions for self-modification"Vein energy emerges here. Pathfinders can use Blooms for fast travel.Go visit Perfumers Avetine and Baboni.Passed the quiz assessmentAt a Pathfinder, you can activate Transporters, restock supplies, report your Aniimo research progress, and heal your Aniimo at the Pathfinder Outpost.Place a level 2 farmland plot in your Home.Upgrade the RV to level 5.Storms once wore down the rocks, lightning carved the cliffs, and time gently healed them, as grass and trees softened the land’s scars.This island seems to belong to the Scar-faced Helgon, but why are there ancient murals of Infergon here? The three stone seats by the shore also seem to appear in the murals. Is it a coincidence, or are there still secrets on this island you have yet to uncover?Show Starry Night Budclaw.Key Eco Spot<localizationIdTag&-2109245546>Ancient ruins divide the yellow and green earth, where the cool tones of the mountains meet the warmth of the plains.Fannie bids you farewell.Cast [Healing Rhythm] to fully recover the Emberpup’s HP.Why does the Helmut hide in its Habitat? Why are they so keen on the “arm wrestling” game?Help the Aniimo find its companion.Explore the story of the BulblyPebbles borne by the wind have scoured the stone for ages, leaving only a patch of primal bareness. In time, they too will crack and fade, until even these marks vanish without a trace.Go to the Mistwoods entrance and search for the fragrance of life.The Jawling Family is known as the “Hoarding Dragon,” fond of securing and guarding treasures. As for Infergon, the Omega of the Jawling Family, what kind of treasure does it cherish?Go check on the seedling.-2031153899Twine with an Emberpup!What secrets do these ancient Lumin Idols hold?Fluffy DMake a call.Chat with the <style=Hint_BgL>scar-faced Helgon</style>.The tenacious Ignitis lies in wait within the shadows.<BR>Respawn interval: 1 minute (spawns at night)Proceed to Bloomville.A Tale of Ice and Fire IIITalk to the shrunken Scorchhowl.Use the wind field to reach the final gate.Give the Popapus some adviceInfergon has been guarding the Sword of Bravery, waiting for its old rival to return. By Twining with Helmut and evolving into Pawney, you are starting to uncover the legend behind the helm and the dragon.Look for the one that looks like cotton candy.Look for the one with a sharp gaze.Defeat Sherro and obtain the spice.Talk to Dr. Lewis.#PlaceholderWhy is Perfumer Awen standing at the foot of the tower?Nicole, look!Dr. Glass's Trial - SusutaA unique Aniimo nest found on the Lost Isles, where you might dig up a precious <style=Hint_BgL>Umbrabow Egg</style>Go to the Dewy nest to brew an aromathyst.Pathfinder OutpostBloom: BlitzwoodListen to the Bolties’ conversation.Alpha Aniimo: RookeyReport to Dr. Lewis.Talk to Bulbly.A Tale of Ice and Fire ICommand your Emberpup to defeat the Celestis!The Elite Pathfinder Challenge is open to the academy's most promising students, with challenges against Elite Pathfinders certified by the academy with outstanding achievements. Successfully passing the Assessment not only proves one's strength, but also earns exclusive Badges and Incredible resources granted by the academy.Go to Echoback Landing and search for the incense of tolerance.Lumin Marking: Veiled TruthHelmut told you that a terrifying "dragon" has been bullying the weaker members of its kind here. Could this be the same dragon from Sorora's story, where "a ghost raised its sword against a giant dragon"? The answer may be waiting deep in the Russet Highlands.The pattern on the s