dentical patterns.A mysterious pattern emerges on the tree.What are these marks?Talk to NovaCancel lock-on.Find a bespectacled NimbiDefeat the First Lethal Thorn.Talk to the Popapus in the contestBecome an official student and claim your reward.Check on the HelmieSave up 140 Home Coins!Defeat the four Lethal Thorns outside.Give the whitesnow rose aromathyst to Awen.Prismana Flow appearsGuide the lost Flutternym out of the MistwoodsApproach the Celestis till it’s within your attack range then start attacking.Day gives way to night, and another new star rises along the shore.Gather information about the mud ballClovis, the young florist, seems to have become friends with a small flower, which has now developed some unknown issues. Clovis might need your help.Find Fannie at the Park and talk to her.Shrubclaw from today's investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Look for Elvira the perfumer at the entrance to Bloomville.Found you!Place 4 Woodland blocks in your HomeBaleetle Jenny stands in the middle of the road, staring at a beautiful mud ball.The Bulbly Family seems to have a unique method for communication. All of this was recorded in the lost research logs.Submit: Treasured Large StarineSmart GreedlingShow Blue Furball's Afternoon.Alpha Aniimo: BlazenFind a <style=Hint_BgL>Cornet</style> willing to join the band.Wake Irisal through battle.Level increased to 35Twine with a Budsquire and hit the Cubbo’s rose.Talk to the Sparkly ShellyAdventurous Cozite - To the Top of the CastleTry using the Emberpup's Fire Bolt to ignite the vinesAn Emberpup and a Bonesky were lifelong rivals in Beast Fang Ridge. They fought 364 duels, and not once did either of them truly win. So they made a promise: once they became Flameruff and Fenrier, they would return to the same place for one final match. But the Emberpup never came. What happened?Lumin Collection: Bounce AwayLumin Marking: Crumbling StonewallsIn 