o the lost Flutternym!An ancient gate rises from the grasslands, its surface etched with primordial designs.Perfumer Marlowe has released a new perfume. Want to try it?Ask Jili what happenedA curious pattern can be vaguely seen through the ice.Find Ranka’s Emberpup.Tell Jeff what you foundOutpost hatchinatorGo to Berylline CausewayTwine with an Emberpup and move to the green target pointAn inactive Bloom Branching. Go there to activate this Bloom.#Placeholder#Investigate the Pranky on the east side of the park.A Broken Helmet?The scar-faced Helgon walks over to one of the stone seats. Is it waiting for someone to arrive?Finish talking to Bohr.Place a Carousel Mill in your Home.Ride the wind to the green target point on the higher platform.Give the flame flower root to Grace.Lively GreedlingVisit the Home.Blend in with the Emberpup familyLumin Marking: Chirpi Songs Over the FjordA Tale of Ice and Fire IVB cuddlesCheck out the upgraded RV Park.Clear the woodland and plant Coconuts.Gather Lumin Amber from the river.The majestic statue seems to be gazing intently at something far awayNimbi from today's investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Challenge Wendell and complete the assessmentBack outside Lumenfly Valley again?Raise your character to level 65.Twine Helmut, shatter the Dragonclaw StoneThe patterns in the ruins flicker in and outBulbly by the CliffAsk Sorora if he has finished his paintings.Talk to the angry FenrierBy observing the electrical patterns of the Bulbly Family, aniimo researcher Sayn noted that they seem to communicate via electrical frequencies. Unfortunately, the research log was lost when he was discovered by the Alpha Luminelle.Own an Emberpup (you can catch one nearby).Deliver the Flame Flower rhizomeYou’ve found the perfumer, Awen.Bouldus's rugged body conceals a will even tougher than stone—never yielding in a collision.<BR>Respawn Interval: 1 minuteProcess an item with the Aniipod Maker once.Keep Twined with the Celestis and glide to the green checkpoint.Lie down.Upgrade the RV's Ecological Module to level 1.Painter of the Russet HighlandsFind the third BubbeepComplete a Home orderTalk to JessicaBridge WidthFind Baleetle Jenny.Take out 3 StarinesBloom: Beast Fang RidgeSprinkle fragrance in front of the seedlings.Pomegg from today's investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Level up to 25Dr. Glass is conducting research on ShelliesObserve the stele.Add the Tubster to the band.Grace hopes you can help find the treasure of the Russet Highlands: the Flame Flower. It seems tied to the legends of the highlands. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to the Russet Highlands and complete the prerequisite quest: Warrior.</style>Where Vein energy surges forth, Pathfinders can fast travel via Blooms.Burn the vines in your way and head to the next checkpoint.Aniimo Researcher Sayn? Sounds impressive! But why is he always sitting there, as if he's not feeling well?Lighthouse?Check: No Echoback SaltAvetine, a perfumer from Bloomville, is offering a high price for an ingredient called Golden Answer. Where could it be? Golden... maybe Blitzwood is worth a look. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Blitzwood and complete the prerequisite quest: An Answer from the Heavens.</style>There is a group of wretched Budsquires near the entrance of Rosetower Woods.Bloom: Nimbus FieldsSwitch to NightThe Sherro of Echoback Landing patrols the narrow coastline with sword and shield in hand, striding across the waves.Prepare to craft fragrance.Raise your character to level 70.Upgrade the RV to level 8.Three ancient monoliths stand, guarding forgotten memories.CalvesAniimo Alpha: TurboCatch up with Nicole—hurry and take a look!Light the incense and open the barrier to Lumenfly ValleyHarvest and pick up 40 Common WheatAt the border between the Susuta and Shelly Habitats, there is a Susuta with a unique temperament.Find the Emberpup that can breathe endless fireThe Helgon and Rookey gathering.Chat with the amazing Jawling.Craft the perfume.Take a look at your Home at night.Challenge Senior Cecelia and complete the assessment.Talk with the First Lethal Thorn.Only at low tide will its full form be revealed.From the Emberpup family's bonfire chatter, you learn that only the strongest Scorchhowl can earn the name "Icho." Many elite Flameruffs have gathered at Thousand-Fang Ridge. Maybe they want to become the next Icho, or maybe they want to restore the Ridgeback Tree to the blazing glory it once had.Talk to the Skippy in the caveFind the second BubbeepFantine, a cheerful perfumer from Bloomville, has often been misunderstood for her optimism. Now she has come to Driftwise Meadow, only to find that she cannot understand why her Nimbi companion is so sad. Is it wrong to be happy? The special perfume ingredient found in Driftwise Meadow may help her find an answer. Find a way to make the Bittersweet Blooms blossom. <style=Hint_BgL>Go to Driftwise Meadow and complete the prerequisite quest: Fentufts and the Nimbi.</style>Alpha Aniimo: TurboThis is ≪J67≫. For details, edit it manually.Bloom: Awaiting ActivationTravel to Voxel SpaceWatch Sunia create the Aeon incense.Give the Flareburst Flowers to Ranka.Investigate the holo projector on the roofMassive stones stand in the woods with bewildering patterns on them hiding the one truth.Ranka, a perfumer from Bloomville, asked you to find his partner: a rather dazed Emberpup. You've heard that Beast Fang Ridge is home to the Emberpup family. Could it be there? And besides being "dazed," what else might Ranka's Emberpup partner be like?Complete the Perfume Journey and restore the colors of the land.Give <style=Hint_BgL>Vine Core</style> to RonTalk to the shopkeeper.View the Warehouse screen.You defeated Tucking. As it fled, a strange Hummin suddenly rushed out and stopped beside the pit, looking around. When you passed by, you heard it muttering to itself. Was that... the language of Idyllians?Deliver the Golden AnswerFind Senior LanaBudsquire from today's investigation list lives near this tracking point. Catch the target Aniimo to complete the investigation and earn points!Omega Aniimo: InfergonThe Blazen is swift as lightning, with every strand of fur standing on end from the electricity coursing through its body.<BR>Respawn Interval: 1 MinuteContinue to craft the perfume with Sunia’s help.Marlowe loves using "strange" ingredients in his perfumes, and he wants your help finding one. But how do you define "strange"? <style=Hint_BgL>Berylline Causeway</style>, famous for its unusual rocks, might be a good place to start.A painter is in trouble.Glow ColorA Tale of Ice and Fire IIKeep talking to Senior LuriaDefeat the Mysterious FigureComplete 4 required quests in Chapter 6.Elven EarsLook for Nimbi at the coffee shop.Can you defeat Alpha Luminelle?Omega at Echoback LandingWith the Shellies' last guardian gone, a group of Susuta has marched straight into Sherro territory. What are they really after?How does one become happy?Return to the dozing BubbeepTalk to the elder.Inner Eye CornersUpper Eyelid AngleHipsChinEye CornersPupil ScaleNose TipNasal Root DepthEyeballsIris HighlightEyelidsCheeksUpper Eyelid FoldForearmsPupil Rotation SpeedLegsLower LipMor—phi!
